n Test:\n\n200 - Requirement for calling Is oxygen sensor at operating temperature. The\ndisplayed voltage signal Is tapped in steps and fluctuates between 0.02 and\n0.85 V. A constant value of 0.45 V Is displayed when the oxygen sensor is not\nworking or lead to DME control unit has a break. This value is also displayed\nwhen no orygen sensor is installed.\n\nCO POTENTIOMETER (Without Catalytic Converter)\n\nFunction Test:\n\n200 - Single-pin plug for CO potentiometer In engine wire harness (on firewall)\nmust be connected. Measure CO. Turn adjusting screw on air flow sensor to ad-\njust to specitied value. Basic setting of potentiometer Is 2.77 V. Refer to 12-152\nfor Specifications.\n\n12-112/8\n\nFAULT LAMP “CHECK ENGINE™ (only USA)\n\nFunction Test:\n\nFault lamp receives 12 V power supply from control unit a3 soon as an exhaust\nrelevant fault Is detected. it lights up continuously after ignition Is turned ON\nfor controlling.\n\nFUEL INJECTORS\n\nElectric Function Test:\n\n300 - Fuel injectors are activated with a frequency of 10 Hz. Pulse time is 1 ms.\nTo avold the ejection of fuel, activation time must be as brief as possible. Acti\nvation can be felt with a hand, Pulses can be checked with a multimeter on the\nfuel Injector plug.\n\nResistance Test;\n\nResistance of a fuel Injector must be measured direct an the component, Only\n@ complete fuel Injector group (2 Injectors) can be measured on DME control\nunit plug. See appendix for specifications.\n\nSENSOR HEATING RELAY\n\nFunction Test:\n300 - This activation takes place in second cycies. Relay remains switched on\nin normal operation for so long, until high speeds or load occur.\n\nPossible Causes of Fault:\n— Lead to DME control unit pin 37 tauity\n- Relay or power supply faulty\n\nCONTROL MASTER RELAY (DME Relay 2)\n\nFunction Test:\n\n100 - Master relay Is activated on terminal 85 with ground potential after Ignition\nIs turned ON or engine runs (display: ON). Relay switches on and supplies reat\nof control unit with power,\n\nPossible Causes of Faull:\n\n- Lead to DME contro! unit pin 54 faulty\n\n— Relay 2 or power supply faulty\n\n— Power supply for DME contro! unit faulty\n\n= Control unit faulty when ground potential is not put out on contro! unit pin\n‘54, although above points are okay\n\nCONTROL UNIT POWER SUPPLY\n\n109 - Control unit has the voltage displayed at the moment. It should not be\nless than 10 V.", "words": [["AIR", 0.0277, 0.0632, 0.0473, 0.0751], ["FLOW", 0.0514, 0.0632, 0.0846, 0.0764], ["SENSOR", 0.0876, 0.0646, 0.1334, 0.0764], ["(LMM)", 0.1375, 0.0659, 0.1697, 0.0804], ["LMM", 0.0257, 0.0935, 0.0493, 0.1153], ["Signal", 0.0574, 0.0935, 0.0911, 0.1153], ["Test:", 0.0947, 0.0935, 0.1193, 0.1153], ["100", 0.0277, 0.1107, 0.0453, 0.1344], ["-", 0.0504, 0.1186, 0.0544, 0.1212], ["Up’Uv", 0.0619, 0.1107, 0.0861, 0.1344], ["value", 0.0921, 0.1107, 0.1193, 0.1344], ["(Up", 0.1254, 0.1107, 0.142, 0.1344], ["=", 0.148, 0.1199, 0.1516, 0.1252], ["potentiometer", 0.1571, 0.1107, 0.2296, 0.1344], ["vottage,", 0.2356, 0.1107, 0.2764, 0.1344], ["Uw", 0.281, 0.1107, 0.2946, 0.1344], ["power", 0.3056, 0.1159, 0.3399, 0.1364], ["supply", 0.3444, 0.1159, 0.3812, 0.1364], ["sv)", 0.4255, 0.1173, 0.4456, 0.1383], ["indicates", 0.0247, 0.1159, 0.075, 0.1555], ["the", 0.0801, 0.1159, 0.0952, 0.1555], ["voliage", 0.1027, 0.1159, 0.1354, 0.1555], ["relation", 0.143, 0.1159, 0.1808, 0.1555], ["resulting", 0.1858, 0.1159, 0.2311, 0.1555], ["trom", 0.2387, 0.1159, 0.2588, 0.1555], ["the", 0.2638, 0.1159, 0.279, 0.1555], ["sensor", 0.2865, 0.1159, 0.3192, 0.1555], ["piate", 0.3268, 0.1159, 0.3494, 0.1555], ["postion", 0.357, 0.1159, 0.3948, 0.1555], ["in", 0.4023, 0.1159, 0.4099, 0.1555], ["CAM", 0.4174, 0.1159, 0.4401, 0.1555], ["Al", 0.0267, 0.1469, 0.0383, 0.1574], ["Idle", 0.0428, 0.1443, 0.0624, 0.168], ["speed", 0.0685, 0.1443, 0.0957, 0.168], ["the", 0.1002, 0.1443, 0.1168, 0.168], ["value", 0.1213, 0.1443, 0.1485, 0.168], ["should", 0.1531, 0.1443, 0.1878